    "text": "To determine how many cookies each child gets, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of cookies the adults eat.\n2. Determine the number of cookies left after the adults have eaten.\n3. Divide the remaining cookies equally among the four children.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the number of cookies the adults eat.\nThe adults eat \\( \\frac{1}{3} \\) of the 120 cookies.\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} \\times 120 = 40\n\\]\nSo, the adults eat 40 cookies.\n\nStep 2: Determine the number of cookies left after the adults have eaten.\nSubtract the number of cookies eaten by the adults from the total number of cookies.\n\\[\n120 - 40 = 80\n\\]\nSo, there are 80 cookies left.\n\nStep 3: Divide the remaining cookies equally among the four children.\nDivide the 80 cookies by 4.\n\\[\n80 \\div 4 = 20\n\\]\nSo, each child gets 20 cookies.\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{20}\\).",
